IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `tlca-dates`
IMPORT `tlca-rules`

-- Limitation Act 1974 (Tas), child abuse claims -- the questions of the SURVIVOR.
--
-- SEAT: the person who was sexually or physically abused as a child and now brings, or thinks of bringing, an action for
-- damages for the injury (or, after a death, the family member or personal representative bringing a Fatal Accidents Act
-- 1934 action for it): "Can I sue at any time?", "By when must I sue?", "Is my time stopped?", "Can I still sue on this
-- day?", "Is what happened child abuse under s 5C?", "Can I reopen the settlement I made?", "What happens to the deed I
-- signed?", "Can they get back what they paid me?", "How much of it can the court count against my damages?". No seat for
-- the court, the person or institution sued, an insurer or the Redress Scheme: the court's orders and judgments are asked
-- as facts.
--
-- Every question takes plain facts (yes/no, dates, numbers, a choice from a list) and calls the rules of tlca-rules.l4.
-- The time bar and the s 5C(5) bar are DEONTIC rules run inside the questions; no question takes a DEONTIC or an EVENT.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Based on material from the Tasmanian Legislation website at 6 November 2026 (c) State of Tasmania, CC BY
-- 4.0; not the authorised version. See SOURCE-LICENSE.md. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Limitation Act 1974 (Tas): the questions of a survivor of child abuse`

§§ `The time limit for a claim about abuse in childhood`
-- Arises only for a person abused as a child, or the family of one who has died ("Has this happened to you?").

@export Can I sue at any time, however long ago it was, for injury from abuse I suffered as a child (Limitation Act 1974 (Tas) ss 5B, 38A(2), 39(1))? Yes for damages for personal injury to you, or a Fatal Accidents Act 1934 claim for your relative's death, arising from or related to sexual abuse or serious physical abuse of you (or them) as a minor, including psychological abuse arising from it -- even if the time limit had run out before 1 July 2018. Not for a claim already out of time before 1 January 1975 (s 39(1)). Otherwise the ordinary 3-year limit applies (s 5A). Another Act's time limit applies instead where it sets one (s 38). A court keeps its powers, for example to stop a case that can no longer be fairly tried (s 5B(3)).
GIVEN `what is the action` IS A `What the action is` @desc What the action is for. One of: damages for personal injury to the person who was abused; damages under the Fatal Accidents Act 1934 for the death of the person who was abused; damages for injury to someone other than the person who was abused; another kind of action
      `what was the abuse` IS A `What the abuse was` @desc What the abuse was. One of: sexual abuse; serious physical abuse; psychological abuse arising from sexual or serious physical abuse; physical abuse that was not serious; psychological abuse alone, or neglect
      `was it while a minor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the abused person was under 18 when the abuse happened
      `did the injury come from it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury (or the death) arose from or is related to that abuse
      `does another Act set the time limit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether another Act sets a time limit for this action (for example a workers compensation scheme); if so, this Act does not apply (s 38)
      `was it already out of time before 1975` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the action was already barred by a time limit before 1 January 1975, under the law in force then (answer no if you are not sure the old law barred it)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I sue at any time for abuse I suffered as a child` MEANS
    `s 5B -- the action may be brought at any time` `what is the action` `what was the abuse` `was it while a minor` `did the injury come from it` `does another Act set the time limit` `was it already out of time before 1975`

@export Is my time to sue stopped for now because I am a "relevant person" (Limitation Act 1974 (Tas) s 26A(4))? It is while you are under 18 and not in the custody of a "capable parent" -- a parent who is not under disability, is not the person you would sue, and cannot be influenced by that person not to sue -- or while you have been unable to manage your affairs because of mental disorder for 28 days or more in a row with no independent legal representative. This matters only where your claim has a time limit (where s 5B does not apply).
GIVEN `am I under 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are now under 18
      `am I in a parent's custody` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are in the custody of a parent
      `is that parent under disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that parent is under 18, or unable to manage their own property or affairs because of mental disorder
      `is that parent the person I would sue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that parent is the person you would sue (for example, the parent who abused you)
      `could a parent be influenced not to sue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that parent, or another parent, may be directly or indirectly influenced by the person you would sue not to bring an action for you
      `incapable for 28 days or more` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been incapable, because of mental disorder, of managing your property or affairs for a continuous period of 28 days or more
      `have I a representative who is not the person I would sue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether someone other than the person you would sue has legal authority to start and run legal actions for you (for example a guardian or administrator)
      `could my representative be influenced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that representative may be directly or indirectly influenced by the person you would sue not to bring an action for you
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is my time to sue stopped for now` MEANS
    `s 26A(4) -- I am now a relevant person` `am I under 18` `am I in a parent's custody` `is that parent under disability` `is that parent the person I would sue` `could a parent be influenced not to sue` `incapable for 28 days or more` `have I a representative who is not the person I would sue` `could my representative be influenced`

@export Can a judge give me 6 years instead of 3 to sue for abuse that has a time limit (Limitation Act 1974 (Tas) s 5A(5), s 38A(3))? A judge may, if he or she considers it just and reasonable -- except where the claim arose before 1 July 2018 and your date of discoverability was before 1 July 2015.
GIVEN `did the claim arise before 1 July 2018` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your cause of action accrued (usually: the injury happened) before 1 July 2018
      `my date of discoverability` IS A DATE @desc The day you knew or ought to have known that the injury had occurred, was caused by the person you would sue and was serious enough to warrant proceedings (while you were a child in a capable parent's custody, what that parent knew or ought to have known counts as yours: s 26A(5))
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can a judge give me 6 years to sue` MEANS
    `s 5A(5) -- a judge may give 6 years` `did the claim arise before 1 July 2018` `my date of discoverability`

@export By when must I bring my action for injury (or a death) from abuse in childhood (Limitation Act 1974 (Tas) ss 5A, 5B, 26(1A), 26A, 38, 38A, 39(1))? Never, if it arises from sexual or serious physical abuse of the person as a minor (s 5B). Otherwise within 3 years beginning on your date of discoverability (6 if a judge has extended it), with the clock stopped while you were a minor not in the custody of a capable parent, or unable to manage your affairs for 28 days or more without an independent representative. Being a child does not otherwise extend the time (s 26(1A)).
GIVEN `what is the action` IS A `What the action is` @desc What the action is for. One of: damages for personal injury to the person who was abused; damages under the Fatal Accidents Act 1934 for the death of the person who was abused; damages for injury to someone other than the person who was abused; another kind of action
      `what was the abuse` IS A `What the abuse was` @desc What the abuse was. One of: sexual abuse; serious physical abuse; psychological abuse arising from sexual or serious physical abuse; physical abuse that was not serious; psychological abuse alone, or neglect
      `was it while a minor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the abused person was under 18 when the abuse happened
      `did the injury come from it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury (or the death) arose from or is related to that abuse
      `does another Act set the time limit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether another Act sets a time limit for this action; if so, this Act does not apply (s 38)
      `was it already out of time before 1975` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the action was already barred by a time limit before 1 January 1975, under the law in force then
      `my date of discoverability` IS A DATE @desc The day you knew or ought to have known that the injury or death had occurred, was caused by the person you would sue and (for an injury) was serious enough to warrant proceedings
      `has a judge extended it to 6 years` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a judge has extended the period to 6 years as just and reasonable (s 5A(5))
      `did the claim arise before 1 July 2018` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your cause of action accrued before 1 July 2018
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
      `was my clock ever stopped` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on or after your date of discoverability, there was a time when you were a relevant person (s 26A): a minor not in the custody of a capable parent, or unable to manage your affairs because of mental disorder with no independent legal representative
      `why was it stopped` IS A `Why the clock stopped` @desc Why. One of: I was a minor not in the custody of a capable parent; I was incapable by mental disorder with no independent legal representative
      `day it stopped` IS A DATE @desc The first day of that time (any date if none)
      `has it restarted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that time has ended (a minor's time ends at the latest when you turn 18)
      `last day it was stopped` IS A DATE @desc The last day of that time (any date if it has not ended)
GIVETH A `The time limit`
`By when must I bring my abuse action` MEANS
    `the time limit for the abuse claim` (`The abuse claim` WITH
        `the action`                          IS `what is the action`
        `the abuse`                           IS `what was the abuse`
        `abused as a minor`                   IS `was it while a minor`
        `arose from or related to the abuse`  IS `did the injury come from it`
        `another Act's period`                IS `does another Act set the time limit`
        `barred before 1975`                  IS `was it already out of time before 1975`
        `date of discoverability`             IS `my date of discoverability`
        `judge extended to 6 years`           IS `has a judge extended it to 6 years`
        `accrued before 1 July 2018`          IS `did the claim arise before 1 July 2018`
        `birth day`                           IS `my date of birth`
        `spell`                               IS (`The spell` WITH
            `there was a spell`  IS `was my clock ever stopped`
            `why`                IS `why was it stopped`
            `spell began`        IS `day it stopped`
            `spell has ended`    IS `has it restarted`
            `spell ended`        IS `last day it was stopped`))

@export If I bring my action for injury (or a death) from abuse in childhood on a given day, is it in time (Limitation Act 1974 (Tas) ss 5A, 5B, 26A, 38, 39(1))? Yes at any time where s 5B applies or while your clock is stopped; yes on or before the last day; no after it, and no for an action already out of time before 1975.
GIVEN `what is the action` IS A `What the action is` @desc What the action is for. One of: damages for personal injury to the person who was abused; damages under the Fatal Accidents Act 1934 for the death of the person who was abused; damages for injury to someone other than the person who was abused; another kind of action
      `what was the abuse` IS A `What the abuse was` @desc What the abuse was. One of: sexual abuse; serious physical abuse; psychological abuse arising from sexual or serious physical abuse; physical abuse that was not serious; psychological abuse alone, or neglect
      `was it while a minor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the abused person was under 18 when the abuse happened
      `did the injury come from it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury (or the death) arose from or is related to that abuse
      `does another Act set the time limit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether another Act sets a time limit for this action; if so, this Act does not apply (s 38)
      `was it already out of time before 1975` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the action was already barred by a time limit before 1 January 1975, under the law in force then
      `my date of discoverability` IS A DATE @desc The day you knew or ought to have known that the injury or death had occurred, was caused by the person you would sue and (for an injury) was serious enough to warrant proceedings
      `has a judge extended it to 6 years` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a judge has extended the period to 6 years as just and reasonable (s 5A(5))
      `did the claim arise before 1 July 2018` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your cause of action accrued before 1 July 2018
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
      `was my clock ever stopped` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on or after your date of discoverability, there was a time when you were a relevant person (s 26A)
      `why was it stopped` IS A `Why the clock stopped` @desc Why. One of: I was a minor not in the custody of a capable parent; I was incapable by mental disorder with no independent legal representative
      `day it stopped` IS A DATE @desc The first day of that time (any date if none)
      `has it restarted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that time has ended (a minor's time ends at the latest when you turn 18)
      `last day it was stopped` IS A DATE @desc The last day of that time (any date if it has not ended)
      `day I sue` IS A DATE @desc The day you file (or would file) the writ or other document starting the action
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I still bring my abuse action on this day` MEANS
    `an action brought on` `day I sue` `is in time under` (`By when must I bring my abuse action` `what is the action` `what was the abuse` `was it while a minor` `did the injury come from it` `does another Act set the time limit` `was it already out of time before 1975` `my date of discoverability` `has a judge extended it to 6 years` `did the claim arise before 1 July 2018` `my date of birth` `was my clock ever stopped` `why was it stopped` `day it stopped` `has it restarted` `last day it was stopped`)

§§ `A child abuse claim I settled before`
-- Arises only for a survivor who settled a claim about the abuse ("Have you settled a claim about the abuse?").

@export Is what happened to me "child abuse" under the Limitation Act 1974 (Tas) s 5C(1), so that an old settlement of it may be reopened? It is sexual abuse or serious physical abuse of you as a child, and psychological abuse arising from it -- but not an act that was lawful when it happened.
GIVEN `what was the abuse` IS A `What the abuse was` @desc What the abuse was. One of: sexual abuse; serious physical abuse; psychological abuse arising from sexual or serious physical abuse; physical abuse that was not serious; psychological abuse alone, or neglect
      `was I a child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were under 18 when it happened
      `was it lawful then` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the act was lawful at the time it happened
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is it child abuse under s 5C` MEANS
    `s 5C(1) -- it is child abuse` `what was the abuse` `was I a child` `was it lawful then`

@export I settled a claim about abuse I suffered as a child: can I ask a court to set the settlement aside and sue again (Limitation Act 1974 (Tas) s 5C(1), (2), (3), (8))? You can if you settled before 1 July 2018, after a time limit on your claim had already run out, and it was child abuse as s 5C defines it. The court sets the settlement aside if it is in the interests of justice, having regard among other things to the amount, the parties' bargaining positions and any oppressive conduct by the organisation before the settlement. Not for an offer of redress accepted under the National Redress Scheme.
GIVEN `what was the abuse` IS A `What the abuse was` @desc What the abuse was. One of: sexual abuse; serious physical abuse; psychological abuse arising from sexual or serious physical abuse; physical abuse that was not serious; psychological abuse alone, or neglect
      `was I a child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were under 18 when it happened
      `was it lawful then` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the act was lawful at the time it happened
      `day I settled` IS A DATE @desc The day the claim was settled (the agreement or deed of settlement was made)
      `had a time limit run out` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a limitation period that applied to your claim before 1 July 2018 had already expired when you settled
      `was it a Redress Scheme offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the settlement was an offer of redress you accepted under section 42 of the National Redress Scheme for Institutional Child Sexual Abuse Act 2018 (Cth)
      `has a court set it aside` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court has already ordered, on your application, that the settlement agreement be set aside in the interests of justice
GIVETH A `What I can do about the settlement`
`Can I reopen my settlement` MEANS
    `s 5C(1), (2), (8) -- what I can do about the settlement` `what was the abuse` `was I a child` `was it lawful then` `day I settled` `had a time limit run out` `was it a Redress Scheme offer` `has a court set it aside`

@export Once a court sets my child abuse settlement aside, what becomes of the settlement agreement and the other agreements that went with it (Limitation Act 1974 (Tas) s 5C(4))? The settlement agreement, and any other agreement relating to the settlement such as a release or a confidentiality agreement, are void to the extent they relate to the child abuse, whatever any other law says -- except a contract of insurance.
GIVEN `has a court set it aside` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court has ordered under s 5C that the settlement agreement be set aside
      `which agreement` IS A `Which agreement` @desc The agreement you are asking about. One of: the agreement that settled my claim; another agreement relating to the settlement, such as a deed of release or a confidentiality agreement; a contract of insurance; an agreement that does not relate to the settlement
      `how far is it about the abuse` IS A `How far it relates to the abuse` @desc How far that agreement relates to the child abuse your claim is about. One of: only to the child abuse; partly to the child abuse; not to the child abuse
GIVETH A `What s 5C(4) does to it`
`What becomes of the agreement once the settlement is set aside` MEANS
    `s 5C(4) -- what becomes of the agreement` `has a court set it aside` `which agreement` `how far is it about the abuse`

@export Once my child abuse settlement is set aside, can the other party get back what it paid me because the agreement is now void (Limitation Act 1974 (Tas) s 5C(5))? No: a party to an agreement made void by s 5C(4) cannot seek to recover what was paid under it on that ground. The section does not deal with recovery on any other ground.
GIVEN `has a court set it aside` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court has ordered under s 5C that the settlement agreement be set aside
      `which agreement` IS A `Which agreement` @desc The agreement under which the payment was made. One of: the agreement that settled my claim; another agreement relating to the settlement, such as a deed of release or a confidentiality agreement; a contract of insurance; an agreement that does not relate to the settlement
      `how far is it about the abuse` IS A `How far it relates to the abuse` @desc How far that agreement relates to the child abuse your claim is about. One of: only to the child abuse; partly to the child abuse; not to the child abuse
      `on what ground` IS A `On what ground it would recover` @desc The ground on which the other party would seek the money back. One of: because the agreement is void under s 5C; on some other ground
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the other party get back what it paid me` MEANS
    `s 5C(5) -- the other party may recover what it paid` (`s 5C(4) -- what becomes of the agreement` `has a court set it aside` `which agreement` `how far is it about the abuse`) `on what ground`

@export If my old child abuse settlement is set aside and I win my new action, how much of what I was paid under it can the court take into account against my damages (Limitation Act 1974 (Tas) s 5C(6), (7))? At most the part that relates to the abuse: all of it if the agreement was only about the abuse; the part the agreement expressly says relates to the abuse; otherwise half of everything paid. The court does so only if it is satisfied that it is just and reasonable.
GIVEN `total paid` IS A NUMBER @desc The total of all amounts paid under the agreement, in dollars
      `was it only about the abuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the agreement related solely to the child abuse your claim is about
      `did it say how much was for the abuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the agreement expressly indicated the extent to which it, and the amounts paid under it, related to the child abuse
      `amount it said was for the abuse` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount the agreement expressly indicated as relating to the child abuse, in dollars (any number if it did not)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much of my earlier payment can the court take into account` MEANS
    `s 5C(6), (7) -- the most the court may take into account` `total paid` `was it only about the abuse` `did it say how much was for the abuse` `amount it said was for the abuse`
